---
title: "5 · Start a case from the template"
description: Start a case from the template on the Cases board and check the tasks it creates.
sidebar:
  order: 6
  label: "5 · Start a case from the template"
---

**Who:** a manager or admin of the department that owns the template, or a partner. Other users see **+ New Case** greyed out; hover over the button to read the reason. **Where:** the department workspace › **Cases**.

## New case

{% steps %}

1. Select **+ New Case**.
2. In **Case type**, choose the template.
3. In **Assigned to**, choose the person in charge, for example Demo Accountant.
4. In **Client**, choose the client, for example ABC PTE. LTD. The client is required when **Needs a client** is on in the template.
5. In **Start**, choose the start date.
6. Select **Create Case**.

{% /steps %}

{% screenshot id="case-templates/case-new" caption="The New Case dialog." /%}

## The case on the board

The case appears in the **Ready to start** column. Its progress shows how many tasks are done, for example `0/7`.

{% screenshot id="case-templates/case-board" caption="The new case on the Cases board." /%}

## The Tasks tab

Open the case and select the **Tasks** tab:

- The template is expanded into its sections and tasks.
- The due dates are worked out as calendar dates.
- A section that must wait for an earlier section shows what it is waiting on. To begin it early, select **Start anyway**.

{% screenshot id="case-templates/case-tasks" caption="The Tasks tab of a case started from the template." /%}
